<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rustĭcŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj.
				dim.</i> [rusticus], <i>rather rustic</i>, <i>somewhat coarse.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Libellus, <i><span class="en">Mart. 10,
			19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomen (Bissula),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. Carm. 7, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> As
				<i>substt.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rustĭcŭ-lus</span></b> , i,
			m., <i>a little countryman</i>, <i>a little rustic</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Sest.
				38, 82</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rustĭcŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f., <i>a little heath-cock;</i> (cf.
			rustica, s. v. rusticus, I. B. 2. b.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 10,
				38, 54, § 111</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 76</span></i>
			<i>in lemm.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
